<title>USA: U.S. cigarette makers buy 618 mln lbs tobacco - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cigarette makers buy 618 mln lbs tobacco - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday said U.S. cigarette makers bought 617.5 million pounds of flue-cured tobacco in the 1995-96 marketing year, up from 463.3 million pounds the prior marketing year.</p>
<p>USDA said purchase intentions for the 1995 crop were 569.9 million pounds and that actual purchases were 108.4 percent of intentions.</p>
<p>Legislation requires each major domestic cigarette manufacturer to purchase an amount equal to at least 90 percent of their stated purchase intentions or face a penalty.</p>
</text>
